<%# Locals: note, field, submitted, response. The lock uses DailyResponse#answered?
    rather than its own length check, so the hint unlocks on exactly the rule the
    progress bar and history use — scaffold labels the user didn't type don't
    count toward it.

    A locked hint is a plain line, and the disclosure is not in the document at
    all: it waits in the <template>, so no key, click or assistive technology can
    open it before the section is attempted. The dashboard script swaps the two
    whenever the answer crosses the threshold, in either direction. %>
<% if note.present? %>
  <% locked = !submitted && !response.answered?(field) %>
  <% disclosure = capture do %>
    <details class="hint">
      <summary>Need a nudge? 💡</summary>
      <div class="hint-body"><%= note %></div>
    </details>
  <% end %>
  <div class="hint-slot" data-hint-for="<%= field %>">
    <p class="hint-locked"<%= " hidden" unless locked %>>Available after you attempt this section</p>
    <%= disclosure unless locked %>
    <% unless submitted %><template><%= disclosure %></template><% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
